# =============================================================================
# Answers for the deploy-e2e workflow's unattended install (issue #133)
# =============================================================================
# Handed to `deploy install --non-interactive --answers-file`. It supplies the
# essential keys the wizard refuses to take a template default for; everything
# else is generated (JWT_SECRET, COOKIE_SECRET, SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY),
# derived (APP_URL, GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL, from --domain) or suggested from the
# runner (JOBS_WORKER_CONCURRENCY, API_MEM_LIMIT, WEB_MEM_LIMIT).
#
# NOTHING HERE IS A CREDENTIAL. Every value is a placeholder on a reserved
# name (RFC 2606 `.invalid`) or a throwaway database password that only ever
# exists inside one runner's `services:` container. The workflow asserts that
# the `e2e-placeholder` values never reach the deploy journal, so the string
# must appear ONLY on keys the CLI marks `secret: true` - a client ID is not
# one of them, which is why GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID below is spelled differently.
#
# THE OBJECT-STORAGE KEYS ARE DELIBERATELY ABSENT. They live in the wizard's
# opt-in `storage` group, and `apps/api/src/config/configuration.ts` defaults
# every one of them to '' rather than throwing at boot, exactly as the `smoke`
# job in ci.yml already relies on. Uploads do not work in this deployment;
# nothing this job asserts goes near them.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The database is the workflow's `services: postgres` container, published on
# the runner's 0.0.0.0:5432 and reached from inside the app containers at the
# docker0 gateway. See the comment on that service: POSTGRES_PASSWORD here and
# the service's own POSTGRES_PASSWORD are one value in two places and MUST be
# kept in step.
POSTGRES_HOST=172.17.0.1
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=e2e-placeholder-postgres-password
POSTGRES_DB=appdb
POSTGRES_SSL=false

# GoogleStrategy hands GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID straight to passport-google-oauth20,
# which throws on an empty string and takes bootstrap down with it - the same
# note ci.yml's `smoke` job carries. Neither value is ever used: no browser
# reaches this deployment and no OAuth round trip happens.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=e2e-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.invalid
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=e2e-placeholder-google-oauth-client-secret

# Whoever logs in with this claims Admin. Nobody ever does.
INITIAL_ADMIN_EMAIL=e2e-admin@e2e.invalid

# Not in any wizard step (it is in the opt-in `observability` group), but an
# existing value is carried through untouched - so this turns the exporter off
# rather than leaving the API retrying an otel-collector that is not deployed.
OTEL_ENABLED=false
